   "postDate": "2026-09-19T20:49:57.963Z",
   "rawMarkdown": "Upon analyzing the cases already labeled in the training set, I notice numerous errors. I see inconsistencies between the report and the case labels, and I cannot overlook the possibility that the test set contains the same errors. Does the test set have labeling errors? Should we design a model that simulates those errors? What is the cause of these errors—are they human errors, or were the labels generated by an LLM?",
   "content": "<p>Upon analyzing the cases already labeled in the training set, I notice numerous errors. I see inconsistencies between the report and the case labels, and I cannot overlook the possibility that the test set contains the same errors. Does the test set have labeling errors? Should we design a model that simulates those errors? What is the cause of these errors—are they human errors, or were the labels generated by an LLM?</p>",
